  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hey , I wanted to suggest suggest. I understand that you guys don't have a fully dedicated individual to the UI and, in-turn, don't touch it as much. I want to offersuggestions the UI\n\nI have found quirks that can be improved specifically to the main menu:\n\nProblems:\n•\tThe current menu feels 2d for vr users\n•\tUI doesn’t have full support for xbox/l controller sticks, forcing mouse use to in order move the cursor.\n•\tUI sensitivity is uncomfortable for desktop users, forcing the user to slow down dramatically to select options, letting user “accidents” happen more commonly by slight movement of the mouse.\n•\tMenu does not follow user vertical movement, causing avatar falling loop where the only exit is to escape the game or when a player opens a menu in a moving station, the menu stays where it was triggered, causing issues to players not to be able to respawn from locked station that’s moving \n•\tAccidentally “unfriend” and “ban” more often\n\nImprovements:\n•\tCompared to standing, sitting is much for helpful for desktop users, the menu feels more comfortable as it is \n•\tRadial Menu allows easier movement tracking and muscle memory\n•\tMore options quickly with an opening menu\n•\tExpandability and customization of menus with “Favorites Page” or “Most Used”\n•\tMenu hooked to capsule rather than location activated, i.e. If the player falls, the menu will be uninterrupted \n•\tThe menu can be re-expanded to follow hexagonal expansions \n•\tthe quick select allows hold-and-release to select options\n\nA good example of this menu is the MGSV quick menu system, where the player can perform quick menu actions quickly and efficiently in the middle of action",
